# The knobs as on the FM-1 (their detents): every click counts, the first after a rest too, so a knob answers at
# once. Only a click straight back within 80 ms of the last is not taken: a detent springing back by itself, not
# a hand (a turn back a tenth of a second later counts). Only a knob that keeps spinning fast goes further: four
# quick clicks in a row (under 70 ms apart) two steps a click, ten three. Choosing (SELECT's rows) is a step a
# click. (HOME's DRONE page: K1 the drone's FILTER, two a step)
knobs real
autoplay 0
wait 300
expect shape11 75
turn K1 1
expect shape11 77
wait 800
turn K1 3 200
expect shape11 83
wait 800
# one too far and straight back, by hand: both count
turn K1 1 100
turn K1 -1 100
expect shape11 83
wait 800
# a detent springing back 30 ms after the click: not taken
turn K1 1 30
turn K1 -1 30
expect shape11 85
wait 800
turn K1 -1 1000
turn K1 -1 1000
expect shape11 81
wait 800
# fast, six clicks: 1 1 1 1 2 2 steps
turn K1 6 60
expect shape11 97
wait 800
turn K1 -6 20
expect shape11 81
wait 800
# a long fast spin: four at 1, six at 2, then 3
turn K1 -14 20
expect shape11 25
wait 800
tap GLO
turn SELECT 6 30
expect row 6
tap HOME
wait 800
# choosing settles harder: ALGO with drone 1's key held, its PLAYS (HELD, AT TIMES, EVERY 2 ..). A setting
# reached, the detent's spring back and its bounce (30 ms apart) change nothing; a turn back after a moment,
# and a steady turn back, every click counts
dswell 0
key b0 down
turn ALGO 1 30
expect dswell 1
turn ALGO -1 30
turn ALGO 1 30
expect dswell 1
expect dtcyc1 0
wait 800
turn ALGO 1 200
expect dtcyc1 1
wait 800
turn ALGO -2 150
expect dswell 0
key b0 up
